From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Towfienes <ngolamtien1706@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:53:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] hyprvx: render the window pass through the camera

Patch 0002 of the HyprVX V3 series (Feature 001, Sprint 1).

- SceneCamera: activeCamera(monitor) is the camera for the monitor's
  window pass, or nullopt for the stock path (identity, no active
  workspace, fullscreen active workspace). cameraRenderModif builds the
  SCALE z + TRANSLATE modifier equivalent to cammath::forward in
  monitor pixels and composes it in front of any geometry modifier.
- renderAllClientsForWorkspace pushes the camera hint before the window
  pass and restores the outer modifier before POST_WINDOWS. The
  special-workspace dim and blur rects are drawn outside the camera.
  No hint when the camera is identity (FR-002).
- RC1: under the camera hint, drawSurface intersects damage with the
  modified window box, transforms the visible-region clip, and
  preDrawSurface transforms the window clip box. Corner radius scales
  with the camera. SRenderModifData gains a hyprvxCamera flag so the
  stock path (including stock geometry modifiers) is unchanged.
- RC2: pass simplification is disabled while a camera applies.
- Borders: renderBorder skips the drawn (modified) window interior under
  the camera hint instead of the logical one; otherwise the border
  disappears where it overlaps the untransformed window box (found by
  the first native zoom run, T040).
- No solitary client and no direct scanout while the camera is not
  identity (reported as SC_TRANSFORM / DS_BLOCK_TRANSFORM).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
